   "text": {
    "L1": "Earth's air, water, soil, forests and oceans are shared by all living things.",
    "L2": "A common myth says pollution in one place cannot affect other places. That is not true.",
    "L3": "Smoke moves with air, so pollution can drift from one city or country to another.",
    "L4": "Rivers carry dirty water downstream, harming people, animals and fields far away.",
    "L5": "Borders on a map do not stop rivers or birds. The Brahmaputra and Amur falcons cross countries.",
    "L6": "Countries and communities must work together to share rivers, protect birds and cut pollution.",
    "L7": "Caring for shared resources helps everyone today and in the future. What can carry pollution far away?"
   },
